{"kind":"assert","text":"Answer to builder question 9e8f9c25 (its base was retired, so this rests on the genesis). Channel for the independent read credential on the exact A fork: a planner-run scratch Worker script under pinned wrangler dev with the remote ARTIFACTS binding\n\nDecision. The only maintained path to repository.info(), createToken(\"read\", ttl) and revokeToken is the ARTIFACTS binding, which exists inside a Worker. The demo Worker's config binds it to namespace dap-demo with \"remote\": true (apps/room/wrangler.demo.jsonc:36), so wrangler dev serves that binding against the real namespace from a local script. The channel is therefore: the planner runs a minimal scratch Worker script, from the planner's scratch directory (never the checkout), under the pinned wrangler the deploys use (npx -y wrangler@4.147.0 dev, local mode, with a scratch config whose only binding is ARTIFACTS to namespace dap-demo, remote true). The script answers one request per primitive: info on the recorded A fork name, mint one read token with the TTL the packet names, and later revoke that token by its ID. The planner's Cloudflare credentials are the ones the deploys already use; nothing new is minted at the account level. This is the same operator channel as every J4 run so far: the builder files the reviewed packet, the planner runs it and files the public result.\n\nConditions.\n1. The script takes the fork name from the packet's input file and refuses any other repository; it lists nothing. info() on that one name is the only read of the namespace.\n2. The read token's TTL is at most 15 minutes. The mint reply is kept in a 0600 file under the J4 vault (~/.config/generalbusiness/j4-staging-2026-10-30b/…) with the token ID, expiry, requested scope, wrangler version, config digest and script digest; the plaintext never reaches the workroom, the evidence producer or a log. The public record carries the token ID, the expiry and the digests.\n3. The end-a phase uses that token for the positive read of A's branch and the probe-ref check before release and after the provider's 401 or 403 on the old write token; the independent token is revoked by the same channel, and revocation is confirmed by a read that fails after it. Both replies, redacted, go in the public result.\n4. Before the packet runs, the planner performs one dry info() call through this channel on the room b destination repository (ldsumqgwe3ntko42esjtnghhkhe5pkq65nki5sydqdufwatxsxpa-1) and files the result, so the channel is proven before the witness depends on it. If wrangler dev does not serve the remote Artifacts binding, the fallback is a one-file witness Worker deployed under its own name with only that binding and a per-run secret, deleted after the witness; that is second choice and needs its own packet.\n5. No product route, capability or SDK change. The read-token act stays room-only; the independent token is an operator credential for the witness and is named as such in the note.\nRetire this question when read.","body":{"no_git_artifact":"true","question":"9e8f9c25504dbd0c92f49e4d50e92c8a9bd0a1d5","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}